Dear Mubbasir Kapadia, Danrui, and Sen,

Our group (Rapid Route) would like to request formal approval for our
semester project concept, revised based on TA feedback.

Project summary: "Dispatch" is an interactive visual simulation of a city's
traffic and emergency response. The core of the project is a realistic
traffic substrate: a zone-based city map where building density drives trip
generation, an origin-destination (OD) matrix distributes trips across
zones with peak/off-peak variation, and a car-following microsimulation
with junction-level right-of-way rules moves hundreds of vehicles without
overlaps or desyncs. Routes are assigned by lowest expected travel cost,
not raw distance. Emergency units (ambulances, fire trucks, police) are
then dispatched through this same realistic traffic, rather than through
hand-waved random congestion.

Selected pillars (changed):
1. Pathfinding & Navigation
2. Swarm & Boids Modeling

Could you please confirm formal approval of this revised concept and let us
know which mentor will be assigned to our group for the semester?

Thank you,
Mihir Shinde (Group Leader)
On behalf of Group Rapid Route

